microscope-importer for Debian
==============================

The .deb carries one binary, /usr/bin/microscope-importer, with every crate
it uses linked in statically, plus a desktop entry that opens it in a
terminal. At run time it drives ffmpeg/ffprobe, udisksctl and lsblk, which
is why ffmpeg, udisks2 and util-linux are dependencies. The font of the note
on black filler (DejaVu Sans Bold) is compiled in.

Building
--------

The source is native (debian/source/format is "3.0 (native)"): the Debian
packaging lives in the upstream git tree in packaging/debian next to the Arch
PKGBUILD. dpkg-buildpackage only looks at ./debian, so stage a copy first:

  cp -a packaging/debian debian
  dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc -b -d

Building needs cargo and rustc 1.85 or newer on the PATH. They are not listed
in Build-Depends because the toolchain is taken from rustup rather than from
the archive; -d tells dpkg-buildpackage to skip the build-dependency check
that would otherwise fail over a cargo that is not dpkg-installed.

cargo is pointed at debian/cargo for its registry cache (CARGO_HOME in
debian/rules), so a build writes nothing outside the source tree. The build
downloads the crates named in Cargo.lock, so it needs network access.

